[{"text":"The propagator may also be raised to integer or symbolic powers","anchor":"cb12-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[StandardPropagatorDenominator[Momentum[p, D], 0, m^2, {3, 1}]]","anchor":"cb13","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(p^2+m^2+i \\eta )^3}\\]","anchor":"cb13-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[StandardPropagatorDenominator[Momentum[p, D], 0, m^2, {-2, 1}]]","anchor":"cb14","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[(p^2+m^2+i \\eta )^2\\]","anchor":"cb14-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[StandardPropagatorDenominator[Momentum[p, D], 0, m^2, {n, 1}]]","anchor":"cb15","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[(p^2+m^2+i \\eta )^{-n}\\]","anchor":"cb15-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Eikonal propagators are fully supported","anchor":"cb15-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[StandardPropagatorDenominator[0, Pair[Momentum[p, D], Momentum[q, D]], -m^2, {1, 1}]]","anchor":"cb16","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(p\\cdot q-m^2+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb16-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[StandardPropagatorDenominator[0, Pair[Momentum[p, D], Momentum[q, D]], 0, {1, 1}]]","anchor":"cb17","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(p\\cdot q+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb17-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynCalc keeps trace of the signs of the scalar products in the eikonal propagators. This is where the \\(i \\eta\\)- prescription may come handy","anchor":"cb17-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[StandardPropagatorDenominator[0, -Pair[Momentum[p, D], Momentum[q, D]], 0, {1, 1}]]","anchor":"cb18","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(-p\\cdot q+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb18-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[StandardPropagatorDenominator[0, Pair[Momentum[p, D], Momentum[q, D]], 0, {1, -1}]]","anchor":"cb19","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(p\\cdot q-i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb19-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"The shortcut to enter FeynAmpDenominators with StandardPropagatorDenominators is SFAD","anchor":"cb19-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[StandardPropagatorDenominator[Momentum[p, D], 0, -m^2, {1, 1}]] // FCE // StandardForm (*SFAD[{{p, 0}, {m^2, 1}, 1}]*)","anchor":"cb20","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Eikonal propagators are entered using the Dot (.) as in noncommutative products","anchor":"cb20-4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[StandardPropagatorDenominator[0, Pair[Momentum[p, D], Momentum[q, D]], -m^2, {1, 1}]] // FCE // StandardForm (*SFAD[{{0, p . q}, {m^2, 1}, 1}]*)","anchor":"cb21","section":"Examples"},{"text":"The Cartesian version of StandardPropagatorDenominator is called CartesianPropagatorDenominator. The syntax is almost the same as for StandardPropagatorDenominator, except that the momenta and scalar products must be Cartesian.","anchor":"cb21-4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[CartesianPropagatorDenominator[CartesianMomentum[p, D - 1], 0, m^2, {1, -1}]]","anchor":"cb22","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(p^2+m^2-i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb22-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[CartesianPropagatorDenominator[0, CartesianPair[CartesianMomentum[p, D - 1], CartesianMomentum[q, D - 1]], m^2, {1, -1}]]","anchor":"cb23","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(p\\cdot q+m^2-i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb23-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"The shortcut to enter FeynAmpDenominators with CartesianPropagatorDenominators is CFAD","anchor":"cb23-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCE[FeynAmpDenominator[CartesianPropagatorDenominator[CartesianMomentum[p, D - 1], 0, m^2, {1, -1}]]] // StandardForm (*CFAD[{{p, 0}, {m^2, -1}, 1}]*)","anchor":"cb24","section":"Examples"},{"text":"To represent completely arbitrary propagators one can use GenericPropagatorDenominator. However, one should keep in mind that the number of useful manipulations and automatic simplifications available for such propagators is very limited.","anchor":"cb24-4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominator[GenericPropagatorDenominator[x, {1, 1}]]","anchor":"cb25","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(x+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb25-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"This is a nonlinear propagator that appears in the calculation of the QCD Energy-Energy-Correlation function","anchor":"cb25-1","section":"Examples"}]